`python3 test_all.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress section took 4.7s); `test_all.py` is untouched.

There were four bugs across the three files:

- **`stats.py` `mean`**: divided by `len(xs) - 1` instead of `len(xs)`.
- **`stats.py` `median`**: for even-length input it returned the upper middle element instead of the average of the two middle ones.
- **`textproc.py` `top_words`**: sorted alphabetically by word instead of by descending count. Ties now keep first-seen order.
- **`seq.py` `dedup`**: appended the duplicates and dropped the first occurrences, the reverse of what it should do.

I re-ran the suite after each fix. The `top_words` bug never showed up as its own failure, because the test's expected answer happens to be alphabetical too, so I fixed it from reading the code.

Nothing is committed; the run also left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
